entries=[('V229','05_team_audit/report_v34/accepted.json','Report version 34 full change audit','The complete diff, new Theorem3.10, exact-tail substitution and all changed numerical claims pass. The ten-row primary table, ratios, eight reflection rows, six finite cutoff values, three reflected cutoff values and uniform coefficients agree with accepted exact endpoints. The updated LP interpretation remains explicitly heuristic.'),('V230','08_improved_upper_bounds/local_projection/strict_increment/phase_uniform_density/verification/accepted.json','Phase-uniform reflected density theorem','Actual lead Note60 independently rederives both density derivatives, monotonicity and convexity, reflection invariance, transverse-angle Jensen comparison, exact transverse integration, normalization and retained cutoff. These agree with the local proof and its symbolic check. This accepts V228 analytically, with no numerical endpoint by itself.'),('V231','08_improved_upper_bounds/local_projection/strict_increment/phase_uniform_density/numerical_values/accepted.json','Directed phase-uniform reflection savings','Eight positive reflection moments are bounded below by64-term sums with an explicit positive geometric remainder. Exact rational coefficients and pi are evaluated at384 and768 bits with different grouping. Each full moment is independently enclosed by an arctangent recurrence inside the series enclosure. All original bases are taken before reflection. New D upper at1/2 is2.6450836612; at3/4 it is3.0973736749. The uniform linear D coefficient on(0,1/100] is2.7249415501. All twelve values improve V226; none claims radius or transport optimality.')]
with (R/'VERIFY_REPORT.md').open('a') as f:
 for lab,rel,title,result in entries:
  d=json.loads((R/rel).read_text());assert d['ledger']==lab and d['verdict']=='CONFIRMED'
  f.write(f'\n## {lab} | {d["time_utc"]} | {title}\n\n**Claim.** The bound or audit identified by the acceptance record is valid within its stated scope.\n\n**Method.** Independent proof comparison, exact endpoint checks and source-hash verification as detailed in the linked standalone proof.\n\n**Result.** {result} Record: {rel}.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED.**\n')
 d=json.loads((R/'08_improved_upper_bounds/local_projection/strict_increment/phase_uniform_density/supplemental_disks/geometry.json').read_text())
 f.write(f'\n## V232 | {d["time_utc"]} | Four supplemental reflection disks\n\n**Claim.** Four additional rational disks per negative-axis pair support additive phase-uniform reflection savings.\n\n**Method.** Wrote the general disjoint-disk proof before computation. Checked all exact separation inequalities and all1280 Bernstein coefficients on256 subintervals for each of four quartic containment polynomials.\n\n**Result.** Geometry passes with strictly positive rational margins. The initial64-subinterval test was inconclusive for the smallest disk;256 subdivisions resolve it. This is a refinement of a lower enclosure, not evidence of failed containment. Full proof and geometry.json are in phase_uniform_density/supplemental_disks. No numerical operator bound is admitted.\n\n**Verdict: OPEN** pending independent analytic cross-read and directed moment evaluation.\n')
p=R/'code/build_verified_table.py';s=p.read_text();old="('08_improved_upper_bounds/local_projection/strict_increment/larger_disks/optimal_axis_disks/numerical_values/accepted.json','V226','eight reflection moments on enlarged axis disks, V226')]:";new=old[:-2]+",\n        ('08_improved_upper_bounds/local_projection/strict_increment/phase_uniform_density/numerical_values/accepted.json','V231','phase-uniform reflected density, V231')]:";assert s.count(old)==1;p.write_text(s.replace(old,new))
